Thank you very much for your time and help. I don't know if my script was not correct, but I changed it based on yours. Here's my old script that the error kept occurring:

library(MSstatsTMT)
library(data.table)
raw.pd <- read.delim("raw.pd.txt")
annotation.pd <-read.csv("annotation.csv")

input.pd.nomiss <-PDtoMSstatsTMTFormat(raw.pd,
                     annotation.pd,
                     which.proteinid = "Protein.Accessions",
                     useNumProteinsColumn = FALSE,
                     useUniquePeptide = TRUE,

                     rmPSM_withMissing_withinRun = TRUE,

                     rmProtein_with1Feature = TRUE,
                     summaryforMultipleRows = sum)

Here's the new script that allow me to get the output:

library(MSstatsTMT)
library(data.table)
pd_tmt = fread("raw.pd.txt")
annot = fread("annotation.csv")

pd = PDtoMSstatsTMTFormat(pd_tmt,
                          annot,
                          useNumProteinsColumn = FALSE,

                          rmProtein_with1Feature = TRUE,
                          summaryforMultipleRows = sum)

I don't know why my old script didn't allow me to get the output using the latest version of R, but I can get the output using the older version of R.

Another question, why should we setting the parameter to FALSE for useNumProteinsColumn in order to get the output but not the TRUE?

I appreciate your help.

